+test_device.py
+==============
+
+Lifetime of the device objects `bluetoothd` creates for remote devices.
+
+test_device_temporary_not_discoverable
+--------------------------------------
+
+:Setup: Two hosts. host0 runs `bluetoothd` with ``TemporaryTimeout = 20``
+	and an agent, host1 has a controller and no `bluetoothd`.
+
+	.. code-block::
+
+		+--------------------+                 +--------------------+
+		| host0              |      BR/EDR     | host1              |
+		| bluetoothd, agent  | <-------------- | btmgmt             |
+		| discovers          |        LE       | connects,          |
+		|                    | <-------------- | advertises         |
+		+--------------------+                 +--------------------+
+
+:Steps:
+	1. host0 calls ``org.bluez.Adapter1.StartDiscovery``.
+	2. host1 opens an L2CAP connection to host0 without pairing and
+	   disconnects.
+	3. host1 advertises connectable reports whose Flags are neither
+	   limited nor general discoverable (``0x18``).
+
+:Expected:
+	1. host0 has a device object for host1 after the connection.
+	2. The device object is removed within ``TemporaryTimeout`` plus
+	   10 s, although the reports keep arriving.
+
+:Notes: Regression test for temporary device objects being kept alive
+	by reports that are not discoverable (`src/adapter.c`). host0
+	alternates scanning and inquiry, which leaves up to about 11 s
+	without any report, so the timeout has to be longer than that.
+
